window.docContents[2].resolve({"/Lean-Code/Saved-Lean-Code/#A-Textbook--Lean-Code--Saved-Lean-Code":{"contents":"The tools in this section come from the Verso namespace TextbookTemplate in the module TextbookTemplate.Meta.Lean.\n\nThe savedLean code block is just like the lean block, except it additionally saves the contents to a file when the book is built.\nThe code is saved to the output directory, in the subdirectory example-code (by default, this is _out/example-code), with its filename being that of the file in which it is edited.\nUse savedImport to save code for the file header.\n\n\n\ndef x : Nat := 15\n\n\nWhen named, the code block's output is saved.\nIt can be both checked and included in the document using leanOutput:\n\n#eval x\n\n\n15\n\n\nExpected error messages must be indicated explicitly:\n\n#eval y\n\n\nUnknown identifier `y`\n\n\n","context":"A Textbook\u0009Lean Code","header":"1.1. Saved Lean Code","id":"/Lean-Code/Saved-Lean-Code/#A-Textbook--Lean-Code--Saved-Lean-Code"}});